From: sunrisepeak <speakshen@163.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 03:55:13 +0900
Subject: [clangd] Say why a module is rebuilt and why a preamble is not reused

A warm start that rebuilds modules it should reuse, or a file whose preamble
is rebuilt for every edit, could only be explained from a verbose log, and
only by inference. Before building a module, clangd now logs at info why the
BMI it had is not reused: none was built for this command and these
prerequisites (and how many were built with others), or the first problem a
reporting read of the stale BMI finds -- the input that changed, as clang
says it. The reporting read happens only on the way to a rebuild, which costs
far more. Why a preamble is not compatible is logged at info too.
